  "decision_conditions": [
    "Proposal is not permitted development due to the proposed extension being more than half the width of the original dwelling (where there is a staggered original rear wall or where the proposal extends beyond the rear wall).  Even with the intent to demolish the furthest forward rear wall (staggered rear wall), case law advises that the 'original' rear wall is the element to be taken into consideration at the time of validation.",
    "The Council consider that the impact of the proposed development on the amenity of the adjoining premises at no.66 Marks Road, would be unacceptable by reason of  excessive depth and height on the shared boundary, resulting in a loss of outlook and an increased sense of enclosure detrimental to the amenity of the occupiers contrary to Policy 7 of the Local Plan and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD 2011.",
    "This written notice indicates that the proposed development would not comply with condition A.4 of Schedule 2 Part 1 Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015.  It is important to note that this written notice does not indicate whether or not the proposed development would comply with any of the other limitations of conditions of Schedule 2 Part 1 Class A.",
    "The applicant has the right to an appeal against this notice to the Planning Inspectorate, see details below."
  ],
